miumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/94/390494/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9bca22b37b8d92a55c02bcb16abbb14cf962b857" commit="6d5fc48fd5c9a772c9389590f60d2e6902dc7190" commit_message="multimedia: Support getting and setting screen orientation  Get/set the screen orientation via using telemetry to open a display setting page and changing the setting.  BUG=b:31608632 TEST=pending  Change-Id: I9bca22b37b8d92a55c02bcb16abbb14cf962b857 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/390495 Commit-Ready: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Cheng &lt;bccheng@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="390495" owner_email="waihong@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/95/390495/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I879cfd559e1d85574c0a0ec1d875b1f1e93a385f" commit="6715e89fb0a1cb67024d9530f556225f739aba8c" commit_message="Add the platform_RotationFps test to measure rotation performance  This test talks to a Chameleon board and a DUT to set up dock mode, change rotation, and measure the fps. In average the rotation animation takes 0.25s to be done. It is about 15 frames on a 60fps monitor.  BUG=b:31608632 TEST=test_that &lt;IP&gt; platform_RotationFps  Change-Id: I879cfd559e1d85574c0a0ec1d875b1f1e93a385f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/390496 Commit-Ready: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chung-yih Wang &lt;cywang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Cheng &lt;bccheng@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="390496" owner_email="waihong@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/96/390496/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7a7ab624e38db19beea38284d3419338dff93d47" commit="969457f6178a72f53b2b6cb77a216b049fd4f92d" commit_message="linux-firmware: stop installing Marvell's 8997 v2 firmware  It's not used and is just wasting space now. It was a preliminary build anyway, and I believe Marvell has settled on the v4 file name going forward.  BUG=none TEST=build, test wifi on Kevin  Change-Id: I7a7ab624e38db19beea38284d3419338dff93d47 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/390757 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="390757" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/57/390757/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia268a186990279377527b7a0f810d1cfc97df469" commit="92fbeaee405db9071a529f58e05b1e5069cd86cf" commit_message="Marvell: drop the 8997 v2 firmware  This was the preliminary filename, and the kernel has switched over to the (final) FW filename *_v4.bin.  BUG=none TEST=build, test Wifi on kevin CQ-DEPEND=I7a7ab624e38db19beea38284d3419338dff93d47  Change-Id: Ia268a186990279377527b7a0f810d1cfc97df469 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/391031 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="391031" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/linux-firmware" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/linux-firmware" ref="refs/changes/31/391031/1" rem