st@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="389691" owner_email="shurst@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/91/389691/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I4f2b989832685c9cd3768ef42c1713fb7fbd29af" commit="6bf2eff6596dcc2a56778b5fffe2f07cc56e0e57" commit_message="CHROMIUM: mesh: fix sta-&gt;addr getting written over  cfg80211_new_mpath passes in a redundant sta-&gt;addr pointer that later gets written over to. sta-&gt;addr is used as the key for the STA rhashtable, so this makes a STA entry inaccessible anymore, and eventually causes kernel to add a duplicate STA entry.  BUG=b:31405056 TEST=manually on a 4 node gale mesh  (cherry-picked from chromeos-3.18 commit 74f2bfbbf0d0 (&quot;CHROMIUM: mesh: fix sta-&gt;addr getting written over&quot;))  Change-Id: I4f2b989832685c9cd3768ef42c1713fb7fbd29af Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/391751 Commit-Ready: Julan Hsu &lt;julanhsu@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Julan Hsu &lt;julanhsu@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Julan Hsu &lt;julanhsu@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="391751" owner_email="julanhsu@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/51/391751/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1b183a80fdee3ec6032af96e95df0401c183a622" commit="147a004859dcf7cd05273f70724357d031315443" commit_message="Don't initialize network controller for gaia login.  BUG=chromium:650936 TEST=login_GaiaLogin  Change-Id: I1b183a80fdee3ec6032af96e95df0401c183a622 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/391123 Commit-Ready: Achuith Bhandarkar &lt;achuith@chromium.org&gt; Commit-Ready: N